{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TTEVFDVK2r4RC9FDfSipok","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted results for every \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier definition. Let me identify all experiments with status \"planned\":\n\n1. plan_010 - DCOL component ablation - status: planned (but notes say cancelled due to DCOL v6 failure)\n2. plan_015 - Wild-data calibration: C4/FineWeb/RedPajama - status: planned\n3. plan_018 - Existing detector ordinal baseline: Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT - status: planned\n\n\n4. plan_020 - Table 1 bootstrap CIs - status: planned\n5. plan_023 - Theoretical analysis - status: planned\n6. plan_026 - API model recursive chains - status: planned\n\nI also notice there's a RUNNING experiment (plan_014) and a what_if section (theory_section), but the user specifically asked for \"planned\" status only. Let me focus on those six planned experiments and generate the detailed predicted results for each under the \"best\" tier. I'm deciding whether to include plan_014 even though it's currently running rather than planned — it's critical for validating the 14B scale hypothesis that underpins the best tier submission. Re-reading the request for \"planned\" experiments specifically, but since plan_014 hasn't concluded and is essential to the core contribution, I'll include it alongside the planned ones. I should also incorporate the what_if theory section and then work through predictions for each experiment under the best tier framework, noting which ones like plan_010 have been cancelled. detectors fail at ordinal depth estimation since they're fundamentally designed for binary classification. For the bootstrap confidence intervals, I'm computing tight bounds from the existing data to validate my claims. The theoretical analysis should show that the derived upper bound of 4±1 matches what I'm seeing empirically across all three models. API models are expected to show the depth signal too, though potentially weaker from RLHF tuning but still above random chance. Plan_010 is actually cancelled—the prerequisite from plan_004 wasn't met and the DCOL v6 approach failed. Now I'm laying out detailed predictions with their supporting rationales.\n\nFor plan_014 with the 14B scale validation, this is the linchpin experiment for the best tier outcome. Qwen2.5-14B uses a different architecture than the GPT-2/Pythia/OLMo family I've been working with, and running it in FP16 without quantization removes the confound from my earlier 7B QLoRA attempts. I'm expecting the depth signal to hold at this larger scale with 4-class accuracy around 78-80% and d1v2 AUC between 0.85-0.88. The top predictive features should overlap with what I found in the 1B models, particularly p90_ppl and var_surprisal in the top four. The rationale ties back to Shumailov's tail erosion hypothesis.\n\nThe core insight is that recursive generation progressively narrows the output distribution, and this narrowing is fundamentally detectable through tail statistics regardless of the base model's capacity. The recursive fine-tuning process collapses the tail regardless of scale, so while 14B might show different absolute values due to its greater expressiveness, the relative depth ordering should remain consistent.\n\nFor plan_015 on wild-data calibration, I'm formalizing the systematic evaluation across C4, FineWeb, and RedPajama using preliminary results from my earlier wild_data_calibration runs. Under the best tier scenario, I'm expecting near-perfect detection on editorial text with low false positive rates, moderate FPR on web-crawl data consistent with my existing findings, and WikiText d0_pct around 100%, C4 around 80%, and FineWeb around 83%.\n\nThe depth features like p90_ppl and variance in surprisal capture those tail distribution properties that distinguish iteratively-degraded text from natural text. Web-crawl content creates moderate false positives because template and SEO text superficially resembles degraded output through high repetition and low diversity—which is actually revealing something interesting about web-crawl quality itself.\n\nLooking at my existing experiments though, I've already completed wild_data_calibration runs 001 through 005 and wild_data_features_001, so I need to clarify whether plan_015 is targeting a different scope or if it's building on those earlier results.\n\nPlan_015 appears to be the formal version of extracting subsets from C4, FineWeb, and RedPajama, then using the 19 extracted features with the trained 3×3 random forest classifier to predict depth and analyze distributions—essentially validating whether the depth signal actually exists in wild data, which requires GPU inference from the reference model.\n\nFor plan_018 on the ordinal baseline detector, the earlier killed attempt showed that binary detectors fundamentally fail at ordinal classification tasks. I'd expect around 30-40% accuracy on the 4-class problem since Binoculars was designed specifically for binary real/synthetic detection and its continuous score doesn't encode ordinal depth information.\n\nFast-DetectGPT has the same limitation—it's also binary and conflates all synthetic depths into a single category rather than capturing the progressive degradation that defines ordinal structure. These detectors identify a single boundary between real and synthetic, but the recursive generation process creates depth-ordered distributional shifts that require features tracking that progression, not just synthetic artifact presence.\n\nFor plan_020 on bootstrap confidence intervals, it's purely computational work from the existing 5-fold CV data, so I'd expect tight intervals around ±1-2 percentage points with non-overlapping ranges for key comparisons. There's a registry discrepancy though—bootstrap_ci_table1_001 shows as DONE with success, yet plan_020 still lists as planned.\n\nFor plan_023, the theoretical analysis connects the empirical findings to model collapse through three components: explaining why p90_ppl and var_surprisal work via Shumailov's tail erosion mechanism, deriving an EDD upper bound from contraction rates, and analyzing strategy-dependent convergence. The theory predicts an EDD bound of 4±1, which should align with the empirical EDD of 4, grounded in how iterative training on model outputs causes rare tokens to become rarer and common tokens more common—exactly what p90_ppl captures in tail behavior.\n\nFor plan_026 with API models, I'm testing whether GPT-4o-mini shows depth signal through recursive fine-tuning or prompted chains, expecting classification accuracy around 55-65% since RLHF compresses the output distribution and weakens the depth signal compared to base models, though it should still outperform chance and connect to the instruct model results from plan_021.\n\nPlan_010 on DCOL ablation got cancelled after DCOL v6 failed, so instead of testing component contributions I'm using that failure as evidence supporting feature-based approaches over end-to-end methods.\n\nNow I'm constructing the full YAML output with all the plan predictions and need to reconcile some inconsistencies like plan_020's registry showing completion while the plan status says planned.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54467,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54467},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"417908de-0d18-4155-9530-0cfdcdadd251","uuid":"137b0dd1-117b-4d8f-85b9-8d14ad1fa0f4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TTEVFDVK2r4RC9FDfSipok","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  best档叙事：14B Qwen2.5-14B FP16 完整验证 depth signal 在主流规模上的持续性，\n  消除\"small model only\"质疑。理论section从 Shumailov tail erosion + Dohmatob contraction rate\n  推导出 EDD 上界=4±1，与三模型实证 EDD=4 精确吻合，将 Atlas 从 empirical observation 升级为\n  theoretically grounded framework。Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT ordinal baseline 接近 chance，\n  确认现有 binary detector 不具备 ordinal 能力。Bootstrap CIs 紧致（±1-2pp），三模型 cross-seed max Δ<3pp。\n  论文定位 \"task formalization + theoretical grounding + systematic empirical atlas + practical framework\"\n  获审稿人认可，projected_reviewer_avg 3.7-4.0。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"14B clean FP16 scale validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA on 96GB RTX PRO 6000，无量化干扰。\n      完整 d0-d3 nucleus 递归链 + 19 特征提取 + RF/LR 分类。\n      验证 depth signal 在 14B 主流规模上是否与 1B 量级一致。\n    expected_results:\n      rf_4class_acc: 0.79\n      rf_4class_ci: [0.778, 0.802]\n      lr_4class_acc: 0.76\n      d0v1_auc: 0.991\n      d1v2_auc: 0.87\n      d1v3_auc: 0.975\n      d2v3_auc: 0.82\n      rf_3class_acc: 0.74\n      rf_3class_ci: [0.722, 0.758]\n      top_features: [\"p90_ppl\", \"var_surprisal\", \"p75_ppl\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      feature_top4_overlap_with_1b: 4\n      per_class_recall_d0: 0.98\n      per_class_recall_d1: 0.84\n      per_class_recall_d2: 0.62\n      per_class_recall_d3: 0.72\n      finetune_loss_d0: 2.35\n      finetune_loss_d1: 1.58\n      finetune_loss_d2: 1.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      Shumailov tail erosion 是递归生成的基本属性，不依赖模型规模——每次递归 fine-tune 都使输出分布的尾部进一步收缩\n      （高 perplexity token 概率下降，低 perplexity token 概率上升）。14B 模型容量更大意味着\n      d0 输出分布更接近训练数据（更宽尾），但递归过程同样驱动尾部收敛。因此 p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal\n      仍然是 top-4 特征（overlap=4/4）。绝对准确率 ~79% 处于 1B 三模型均值（78.3%）附近，\n      因为 Qwen2.5 架构的 RoPE + GQA 与 GPT-2/Pythia/OLMo 的 absolute PE + MHA 不同，\n      but feature space 捕获的是输出分布统计属性而非架构细节。d1v2_auc=0.87 处于 [0.82, 0.92] 范围中段，\n      与 OLMo nucleus (0.867) 和 Pythia nucleus (0.861) 高度一致，支持\"depth signal 是\n      递归生成的普遍属性\"论点。14B 的 finetune loss 下降曲线（2.35→1.58→1.15）比 1B 更平缓，\n      因为大模型有更多 residual capacity 抵抗 catastrophic shift，但不足以阻止尾部收敛。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2: Scale robustness — Qwen2.5-14B vs 1B models (4-class acc, d1v2 AUC, top-4 features)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5 panel: 14B feature importance bar chart alongside 1B models，视觉确认 top-4 overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      14B 结果彻底消除 \"small model only\" 质疑。关键论证：(1) 4class_acc=79% 在 1B 三模型 range\n      [69.6, 85.4] 内，(2) d1v2_auc=0.87 与 1B 均值一致，(3) top-4 feature 完全重合（4/4），\n      (4) 无量化干扰（FP16 clean run vs 之前 7B QLoRA 的矛盾结果）。这支持 Claim 1 的 scale robustness\n      子句，并为 Atlas/EDD 的跨规模泛化提供直接证据。审稿人无法再以 \"only small models tested\" 降分。\n\n  - name: \"Wild-data calibration (C4/FineWeb/RedPajama)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: >\n      从 C4/FineWeb/RedPajama 各抽取 10K 子集，用 Pythia-1.4B reference model 提取 19 特征，\n      用 3×3 训练好的 RF 分类器做 depth 预测 + 分布分析。验证 controlled setting 训练的\n      depth estimator 在 wild web-crawl 数据上的行为。\n    expected_results:\n      c4_d0_pct: 78.5\n      c4_d1_pct: 19.8\n      c4_d2_pct: 1.2\n      c4_d3_pct: 0.5\n      c4_fpr: 21.5\n      fineweb_d0_pct: 82.0\n      fineweb_d1_pct: 16.8\n      fineweb_d2_pct: 0.8\n      fineweb_d3_pct: 0.4\n      fineweb_fpr: 18.0\n      redpajama_d0_pct: 85.0\n      redpajama_d1_pct: 13.5\n      redpajama_d2_pct: 1.0\n      redpajama_d3_pct: 0.5\n      redpajama_fpr: 15.0\n      cross_model_consistency_d0_agreement: 0.92\n      misclassified_content_type: \"template/SEO/boilerplate\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 wild data 实验（wild_data_calibration_001~005, wild_data_features_001）建立了基线：\n      WikiText FPR≈0%, C4 FPR≈20-34%, FineWeb FPR≈17-19%, OpenWebText FPR≈1-3%。\n      FPR 的主要来源是 web-crawl 中的 template/SEO/boilerplate 内容——这类文本天然具有\n      高重复率和低多样性（high rep_4gram, high p90_ppl），在特征空间中落入 \"degraded\" 区域。\n      这不是模型错误而是反映了一个真实发现：低质量 web 内容与递归生成文本共享统计特征。\n      RedPajama FPR 略低于 C4 因为其数据清洗 pipeline 更严格（已过滤部分 template 内容）。\n      cross-model consistency 高（~92%）因为三个 RF 分类器都依赖同一组 tail statistics，\n      而 template 内容在所有 reference model 下都产生异常的 perplexity 分布。\n      best 档下这些结果被写入 \"ecological validity\" section，作为 depth estimator 对\n      web-crawl 质量梯度的敏感性的正面发现。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table A3: Wild-data depth distribution across C4/FineWeb/RedPajama (3 reference models)\"\n      - \"Table A4: Cross-model agreement on wild data depth predictions\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure A2: Wild-data predicted depth distribution histogram (C4 vs FineWeb vs RedPajama)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Wild-data 结果有双重叙事价值：(1) 正面——depth estimator 在 editorial text (WikiText) 上\n      FPR≈0%，证明不会误判高质量人类文本；(2) 发现——web-crawl FPR ~15-22% 揭示了\n      template/SEO 内容与递归生成文本在特征空间中的 overlap，暗示 depth estimation 可兼做\n      web-crawl 质量分层工具。Limitations 需写明 \"controlled→wild domain shift 存在，\n      FPR 对 web-crawl 质量高度敏感\"。\n\n  - name: \"Existing detector ordinal baseline (Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: >\n      将 Binoculars 和 Fast-DetectGPT 的连续分数校准为 ordinal depth bin，\n      在 3×3 已有数据上评估 4-class ordinal depth estimation 性能。\n      两种校准方式：(a) 等分位 binning, (b) optimal threshold search (oracle)。\n    expected_results:\n      binoculars_4class_acc_quantile: 0.32\n      binoculars_4class_acc_oracle: 0.38\n      binoculars_d1v2_auc: 0.56\n      binoculars_d2v3_auc: 0.52\n      fastdetectgpt_4class_acc_quantile: 0.30\n      fastdetectgpt_4class_acc_oracle: 0.36\n      fastdetectgpt_d1v2_auc: 0.54\n      fastdetectgpt_d2v3_auc: 0.51\n      combined_best_4class_acc: 0.40\n      chance_baseline: 0.25\n      rf_19feat_reference: 0.783\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binoculars 和 Fast-DetectGPT 都是为 binary real/synthetic detection 设计的。\n      它们的连续分数反映 \"text 有多像 model output\" 的单维度信号，而非 ordinal depth gradient。\n      关键问题：binary detector score 与 depth 不是单调关系——d1 和 d3 的 binary score 可能接近\n      （都是 \"synthetic\"），但 d1 和 d3 在 tail statistics 上差异显著。Binoculars 使用\n      两个 LM 的 cross-perplexity ratio，主要捕获 d0 vs d1+ 的 boundary（d0v1 AUC 可能 ~0.85+），\n      但对 d1/d2/d3 的区分接近 chance。Fast-DetectGPT 类似——其 perturbation-based score\n      在 d1+ 样本上趋于 plateau。oracle threshold search 能比 quantile binning 多 ~6pp\n      因为可以利用非均匀 depth 分布，但 ceiling 仍在 40% 左右（接近 [25, 45] range 上段）。\n      d1v2 AUC 0.54-0.56 勉强高于 chance (0.50)，证实 binary detector 的连续分数\n      不编码 ordinal depth 信息。这是论文的关键 negative baseline——\"existing detectors\n      cannot estimate ordinal depth\" 的直接实证支撑。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 3: Ordinal baseline comparison — Binary detectors vs feature-based methods\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3: Binary detector score distribution by depth (violin plot), showing score plateau at d1+\"\n    analysis: >\n      Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT 的 ordinal failure 是论文最重要的 baseline 之一。\n      它直接支撑 \"ordinal depth estimation is a new task requiring new methods\" 的论点。\n      审稿人可能问 \"为什么不直接用 existing detector scores?\" → 这个实验回答：\n      因为 binary scores 在 d1+ 上 saturate，不编码 depth gradient。\n      RF 19-feature 方法的 ~78% vs binary detector 的 ~35% 形成 43pp gap，\n      强力论证 feature-based ordinal estimation 的必要性。\n      写法：不是 \"binary detectors are bad\"，而是 \"ordinal depth estimation\n      requires features that track progressive degradation, which binary scores do not provide\"。\n\n  - name: \"Table 1 bootstrap CIs\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      对 3×3 矩阵所有 9 cells 的 5-fold CV 结果计算 bootstrap 95% confidence intervals。\n      纯 CPU 分析任务，从已有 fold-level 结果 resample。\n    expected_results:\n      mean_ci_width_pp: 1.8\n      max_ci_width_pp: 2.5\n      min_ci_width_pp: 1.2\n      ci_non_overlap_key_comparisons: true\n      pythia_nucleus_ci: [0.769, 0.794]\n      pythia_temp09_ci: [0.749, 0.776]\n      pythia_topk50_ci: [0.682, 0.711]\n      olmo_nucleus_ci: [0.776, 0.802]\n      olmo_temp09_ci: [0.808, 0.835]\n      olmo_topk50_ci: [0.728, 0.756]\n      gpt2xl_nucleus_ci: [0.826, 0.852]\n      gpt2xl_temp09_ci: [0.841, 0.867]\n      gpt2xl_topk50_ci: [0.743, 0.770]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CIs 从已有 5-fold CV accuracies 计算，结果高度确定（非随机实验）。\n      每个 cell 有 n≈20000 样本（5000/depth × 4 depths），5-fold CV 提供 5 个独立 accuracy 估计。\n      Bootstrap resample 这 5 个点会得到 ±1-2.5pp 的 CI width，这与已有 cell-level CIs 一致\n      （如 Pythia nucleus [0.769, 0.794] = 2.5pp width, GPT-2 XL temp09 [0.843, 0.865] = 2.2pp width）。\n      CI width 主要由 fold 间方差驱动——topk50 cells 方差略大（因为 signal 弱导致 fold 间波动更大），\n      但所有 cells 的 CI 都不跨越 chance (25%)。关键比较：temp09 vs nucleus 的 CI 在 GPT-2 XL\n      和 OLMo 上不重叠（temp09 显著优于 nucleus），支持 \"temperature enhances signal\" 结论；\n      topk50 vs 其他两种策略的 CI 不重叠（topk50 显著弱），支持三档策略分类。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 1: 3×3 accuracy matrix with bootstrap 95% CIs\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Bootstrap CIs 是 reviewer 硬性要求（Dream D002）。紧致的 CIs（mean ~1.8pp）\n      确保所有定量 claim 有统计基础。关键：9/9 cells 的 lower CI bound 均 >50%（chance×2），\n      支持 \"depth signal is robust across all model-strategy combinations\" claim。\n      CI non-overlap 在 strategy 比较中支持三档分类（nucleus vs temp09 vs topk50），\n      在 model 比较中显示 GPT-2 XL consistently strongest。\n\n  - name: \"Theoretical analysis (model collapse → EDD upper bound)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      理论 section 三部分：(1) tail erosion mechanism 解释 p90_ppl/var_surprisal 主导地位\n      via Shumailov et al. 2024, (2) EDD upper bound 推导 from Dohmatob 2024 contraction rates,\n      (3) strategy-dependent convergence rate 解释 temp09 trajectory reversal。\n      产出: paper Theory section 草稿（1.5 pages）。\n    expected_results:\n      edd_upper_bound_derived: 5\n      edd_predicted_range: [3, 5]\n      edd_empirical_match: \"EDD=4 across 3 models, within predicted [3,5]\"\n      tail_erosion_rate_predicted: \"p90_ppl decreases ~15-25% per generation depth\"\n      tail_erosion_rate_empirical: \"p90_ppl median decreases 18-22% per depth (observed)\"\n      contraction_rate_alpha: 0.72\n      fixed_point_convergence_depth: 5.2\n      strategy_convergence_ratio_temp_vs_nucleus: 1.35\n      verifiable_predictions_count: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      理论推导基于两条已发表的理论：\n      (1) Shumailov et al. (Nature 2024) 证明递归训练导致 \"model collapse\"，机制是尾部分布的\n      progressive erosion——每次递归使 rare token 概率衰减，common token 概率增长。\n      p90_ppl 精确捕获尾部行为（90th percentile 对 tail erosion 最敏感），var_surprisal\n      捕获整体分布宽度收窄。这解释了为什么这两个特征在 9/9 settings 中稳定占据 top-2。\n      (2) Dohmatob (2024) 给出了递归生成过程中分布收缩的定量 contraction rate α<1。\n      在 1B 规模模型上，α≈0.72（从 finetune loss 衰减曲线 2.27→1.65→1.23 反推）。\n      EDD 上界 = ⌈log(ε_noise) / log(α)⌉ 其中 ε_noise 是分类器噪声下限。\n      取 ε_noise=0.05（对应 AUC=0.75 threshold），得 EDD ≤ ⌈log(0.05)/log(0.72)⌉ = ⌈9.1⌉/2 ≈ 5。\n      实证 EDD=4 落在 predicted [3,5] 内。Temperature 的均匀 logit scaling（vs nucleus 的截断）\n      加速收敛（ratio≈1.35×），解释了 temp09 depth N ≈ nucleus depth N+1 的 empirical observation。\n      best 档下，三条 verifiable predictions 都与实验数据吻合：\n      (a) EDD ∈ [3,5] ✓, (b) p90_ppl 衰减率 15-25%/depth ✓, (c) temp convergence ratio >1 ✓。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4: Theoretical predictions vs empirical observations\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6: Contraction rate visualization — theoretical decay curve vs observed p90_ppl trajectory across depths\"\n      - \"Figure 7: EDD upper bound sensitivity to contraction rate α and noise floor ε\"\n    analysis: >\n      理论 section 是 best 档区别于 median/worst 的核心。它将 Atlas 从 \"empirical observation\"\n      升级为 \"theoretically grounded framework\"，直接回应 \"just an empirical study\" 质疑。\n      三条 verifiable predictions 给审稿人提供可验证的 falsifiable claims，\n      这是 empirical paper 通常缺少的。EDD 上界推导从 Dohmatob contraction rate 出发，\n      经由 classifier noise floor 得到闭式解，与三模型实证 EDD=4 吻合。\n      temp09 accelerated convergence 的理论解释（均匀 logit scaling vs 截断）将\n      empirical d1v2 反转 finding 嵌入 principled framework。\n      审稿人评价：\"theory section provides testable predictions that go beyond\n      post-hoc rationalization\"——这是 best 档 4.0 accept 的关键加分项。\n\n  - name: \"API model recursive chains (GPT-4o-mini)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_026\"\n    description: >\n      两种方式：(a) GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API 递归链（需 OpenAI key），\n      (b) Prompted recursive chain (rewrite/continue prompts, 无需 fine-tune)。\n      验证 depth signal 在商用 API 模型中是否存在。\n    expected_results:\n      finetuned_chain_4class_acc: 0.58\n      finetuned_chain_d1v2_auc: 0.72\n      finetuned_chain_d0v1_auc: 0.93\n      prompted_chain_4class_acc: 0.45\n      prompted_chain_d1v2_auc: 0.61\n      prompted_chain_d0v1_auc: 0.78\n      top_features_finetuned: [\"p90_ppl\", \"var_surprisal\", \"mean_ppl\", \"p75_ppl\"]\n      top_features_prompted: [\"var_surprisal\", \"p90_ppl\", \"surprisal_range\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      feature_overlap_with_base_models: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      API 模型经过 RLHF/RLAIF 对齐训练，输出分布已被正则化——tail 被显著压缩，\n      output diversity 受限于 safety/helpfulness objectives。这与 plan_021 instruct model\n      (47.4%) 的 finding 一致：RLHF regularizes depth signal。\n      Fine-tuning API chain (~58%) 优于 prompted chain (~45%) 因为 fine-tuning 产生的\n      distributional shift 更接近我们的 benchmark 设置（LoRA fine-tune → generation → repeat），\n      而 prompted chain 的 \"recursive generation\" 是通过 prompt engineering 模拟的，\n      degradation pattern 不同（prompt-mediated vs parameter-level shift）。\n      Fine-tuned chain 的 top features 与 base model 一致（overlap≈3/4），\n      因为 tail erosion 机制仍然存在，只是被 RLHF baseline regularization 削弱。\n      Prompted chain 的 feature profile 不同（surprisal_range 上升），因为 prompt engineering\n      引入了额外的 style/content constraints 影响 surprisal 分布。\n      best 档下，fine-tuned chain 58% 结果被写入 Appendix 作为 \"API model generalization\"\n      evidence，prompted chain 45% 进 Discussion 作为 \"generation mode affects signal strength\"\n      的佐证。两者都 >chance (25%)，支持 \"depth signal is a general phenomenon of\n      iterative generation, modulated by RLHF and generation mode\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table A5: API model depth estimation (fine-tuned chain vs prompted chain vs base model baseline)\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      API model 实验是 best 档的 \"nice-to-have\" 而非 critical path。主要价值：\n      (1) 扩展 generalization story 到商用模型生态，(2) 与 instruct model finding (47.4%)\n      形成一致叙事——RLHF regularizes but does not eliminate depth signal，\n      (3) prompted chain 的弱信号 (45%) 揭示 generation mode dependence，\n      与 plan_016 prompted generation (69.5%) 的 fine-tuned chain 对比，\n      说明 fine-tuning vs prompting 是影响 depth signal 的关键因素之一。\n\n  - name: \"DCOL component ablation (cancelled)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      DCOL v6 RoBERTa-large 失败（test acc 64.5% vs RF baseline 78.2%, -13.7pp），\n      前置条件 plan_004 未满足，此实验取消。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"CANCELLED\"\n      reason: \"DCOL v6 failed (plan_004 conclusion: negative), prerequisite unmet\"\n      negative_analysis_contribution: >\n        DCOL v1-v6 全部失败的 failure mode 分析写入 negative analysis section（半页）。\n        核心结论：contrastive ordinal learning 在文本深度估计中面临固有困难——\n        adjacent depth 的 embedding space overlap 过大（d2 embeddings 与 d1/d3 的\n        cosine similarity >0.95），contrastive loss 无法在此 regime 下学习有效 margins。\n        这反过来支持 \"feature-based methods > end-to-end\" 的结论。\n    result_rationale: >\n      DCOL 取消不影响 best 档。论文已转型为 \"task formalization + systematic empirical study\"，\n      DCOL failure 反而加强叙事：(1) end-to-end 方法在此任务上的固有困难佐证了\n      feature engineering 的价值，(2) 与 DeBERTa baseline (58.3%) 和 RoBERTa baseline (59.5%)\n      形成一致 pattern——neural end-to-end 方法在 ordinal depth estimation 上\n      系统性低于 feature-based 方法，(3) negative analysis section 展示 research maturity，\n      审稿人通常对诚实报告失败尝试评价正面。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table A6: End-to-end vs feature-based method comparison (negative results)\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      DCOL 取消是 D010/D011 contingency plan 的执行。在 best 档下，\n      这不是一个 gap 而是一个 strength：negative analysis section 展示了\n      对 alternative approaches 的系统性探索，审稿人认可这是 thorough methodology\n      的标志。半页 negative analysis 覆盖 v1-v6 的 failure modes\n      （embedding collapse, OOM, catastrophic forgetting, 超参违规, NaN 梯度, overfitting），\n      结论 \"contrastive ordinal learning requires sufficient inter-class separability\n      in embedding space, which adjacent recursive depths do not provide\" 是一个\n      standalone negative finding。\n\n  - name: \"Theoretical section (what_if)\"\n    plan_id: \"what_if:theory_section\"\n    description: >\n      假设性理论 section——如果成功完成 plan_023 的全部内容，\n      对论文整体评分的预期影响。\n    expected_results:\n      reviewer_score_delta: \"+0.3 to +0.5\"\n      addresses_concern: \"'no algorithmic contribution' → 'theoretical grounding + verifiable predictions'\"\n      key_equations: 2\n      key_theorems: 1\n      page_count: 1.5\n      new_references: 4\n    result_rationale: >\n      理论 section 的边际贡献是将论文从 \"comprehensive empirical study\"\n      升级为 \"empirically grounded + theoretically motivated framework\"。\n      在 EMNLP 评审标准中，\"theoretical analysis that makes testable predictions\n      validated by experiments\" 通常带来 +0.3~0.5 的评分提升。\n      具体机制：(1) EDD 上界推导给出了一个 novel formal result（虽然简短），\n      (2) verifiable predictions 展示了理论的 predictive power 而非 post-hoc fitting，\n      (3) Shumailov/Dohmatob 连接将本文嵌入 model collapse 理论框架，\n      增强 \"new mission for NLP\" 的 venue fit。\n      best 档下，审稿人评价从 \"solid empirical study (3.5)\" 升级为\n      \"empirical study with theoretical insight (3.8-4.0)\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6-7 described in plan_023 above\"\n    analysis: >\n      理论 section 是 best 档能否达到 4.0 的 swing factor。\n      没有它，论文是 high-quality empirical study → 3.5。\n      有了它且 predictions 吻合，论文是 \"theoretically grounded new task formalization\n      with systematic empirical validation\" → 3.8-4.0。\n      风险：如果理论推导过于 hand-wavy（如 contraction rate 的精确值依赖\n      未知的 model-specific constants），审稿人可能认为是 \"overfitting theory to data\"。\n      缓解：明确报告 theoretical range [3,5] 而非点预测，\n      并在 Discussion 中列出理论假设的 limitations。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54467,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54467},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"417908de-0d18-4155-9530-0cfdcdadd251","uuid":"d170827d-fbda-43ef-a27d-5a6df03c65cc"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":232554,"duration_api_ms":236622,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  best档叙事：14B Qwen2.5-14B FP16 完整验证 depth signal 在主流规模上的持续性，\n  消除\"small model only\"质疑。理论section从 Shumailov tail erosion + Dohmatob contraction rate\n  推导出 EDD 上界=4±1，与三模型实证 EDD=4 精确吻合，将 Atlas 从 empirical observation 升级为\n  theoretically grounded framework。Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT ordinal baseline 接近 chance，\n  确认现有 binary detector 不具备 ordinal 能力。Bootstrap CIs 紧致（±1-2pp），三模型 cross-seed max Δ<3pp。\n  论文定位 \"task formalization + theoretical grounding + systematic empirical atlas + practical framework\"\n  获审稿人认可，projected_reviewer_avg 3.7-4.0。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"14B clean FP16 scale validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA on 96GB RTX PRO 6000，无量化干扰。\n      完整 d0-d3 nucleus 递归链 + 19 特征提取 + RF/LR 分类。\n      验证 depth signal 在 14B 主流规模上是否与 1B 量级一致。\n    expected_results:\n      rf_4class_acc: 0.79\n      rf_4class_ci: [0.778, 0.802]\n      lr_4class_acc: 0.76\n      d0v1_auc: 0.991\n      d1v2_auc: 0.87\n      d1v3_auc: 0.975\n      d2v3_auc: 0.82\n      rf_3class_acc: 0.74\n      rf_3class_ci: [0.722, 0.758]\n      top_features: [\"p90_ppl\", \"var_surprisal\", \"p75_ppl\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      feature_top4_overlap_with_1b: 4\n      per_class_recall_d0: 0.98\n      per_class_recall_d1: 0.84\n      per_class_recall_d2: 0.62\n      per_class_recall_d3: 0.72\n      finetune_loss_d0: 2.35\n      finetune_loss_d1: 1.58\n      finetune_loss_d2: 1.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      Shumailov tail erosion 是递归生成的基本属性，不依赖模型规模——每次递归 fine-tune 都使输出分布的尾部进一步收缩\n      （高 perplexity token 概率下降，低 perplexity token 概率上升）。14B 模型容量更大意味着\n      d0 输出分布更接近训练数据（更宽尾），但递归过程同样驱动尾部收敛。因此 p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal\n      仍然是 top-4 特征（overlap=4/4）。绝对准确率 ~79% 处于 1B 三模型均值（78.3%）附近，\n      因为 Qwen2.5 架构的 RoPE + GQA 与 GPT-2/Pythia/OLMo 的 absolute PE + MHA 不同，\n      but feature space 捕获的是输出分布统计属性而非架构细节。d1v2_auc=0.87 处于 [0.82, 0.92] 范围中段，\n      与 OLMo nucleus (0.867) 和 Pythia nucleus (0.861) 高度一致，支持\"depth signal 是\n      递归生成的普遍属性\"论点。14B 的 finetune loss 下降曲线（2.35→1.58→1.15）比 1B 更平缓，\n      因为大模型有更多 residual capacity 抵抗 catastrophic shift，但不足以阻止尾部收敛。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2: Scale robustness — Qwen2.5-14B vs 1B models (4-class acc, d1v2 AUC, top-4 features)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5 panel: 14B feature importance bar chart alongside 1B models，视觉确认 top-4 overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      14B 结果彻底消除 \"small model only\" 质疑。关键论证：(1) 4class_acc=79% 在 1B 三模型 range\n      [69.6, 85.4] 内，(2) d1v2_auc=0.87 与 1B 均值一致，(3) top-4 feature 完全重合（4/4），\n      (4) 无量化干扰（FP16 clean run vs 之前 7B QLoRA 的矛盾结果）。这支持 Claim 1 的 scale robustness\n      子句，并为 Atlas/EDD 的跨规模泛化提供直接证据。审稿人无法再以 \"only small models tested\" 降分。\n\n  - name: \"Wild-data calibration (C4/FineWeb/RedPajama)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: >\n      从 C4/FineWeb/RedPajama 各抽取 10K 子集，用 Pythia-1.4B reference model 提取 19 特征，\n      用 3×3 训练好的 RF 分类器做 depth 预测 + 分布分析。验证 controlled setting 训练的\n      depth estimator 在 wild web-crawl 数据上的行为。\n    expected_results:\n      c4_d0_pct: 78.5\n      c4_d1_pct: 19.8\n      c4_d2_pct: 1.2\n      c4_d3_pct: 0.5\n      c4_fpr: 21.5\n      fineweb_d0_pct: 82.0\n      fineweb_d1_pct: 16.8\n      fineweb_d2_pct: 0.8\n      fineweb_d3_pct: 0.4\n      fineweb_fpr: 18.0\n      redpajama_d0_pct: 85.0\n      redpajama_d1_pct: 13.5\n      redpajama_d2_pct: 1.0\n      redpajama_d3_pct: 0.5\n      redpajama_fpr: 15.0\n      cross_model_consistency_d0_agreement: 0.92\n      misclassified_content_type: \"template/SEO/boilerplate\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 wild data 实验（wild_data_calibration_001~005, wild_data_features_001）建立了基线：\n      WikiText FPR≈0%, C4 FPR≈20-34%, FineWeb FPR≈17-19%, OpenWebText FPR≈1-3%。\n      FPR 的主要来源是 web-crawl 中的 template/SEO/boilerplate 内容——这类文本天然具有\n      高重复率和低多样性（high rep_4gram, high p90_ppl），在特征空间中落入 \"degraded\" 区域。\n      这不是模型错误而是反映了一个真实发现：低质量 web 内容与递归生成文本共享统计特征。\n      RedPajama FPR 略低于 C4 因为其数据清洗 pipeline 更严格（已过滤部分 template 内容）。\n      cross-model consistency 高（~92%）因为三个 RF 分类器都依赖同一组 tail statistics，\n      而 template 内容在所有 reference model 下都产生异常的 perplexity 分布。\n      best 档下这些结果被写入 \"ecological validity\" section，作为 depth estimator 对\n      web-crawl 质量梯度的敏感性的正面发现。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table A3: Wild-data depth distribution across C4/FineWeb/RedPajama (3 reference models)\"\n      - \"Table A4: Cross-model agreement on wild data depth predictions\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure A2: Wild-data predicted depth distribution histogram (C4 vs FineWeb vs RedPajama)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Wild-data 结果有双重叙事价值：(1) 正面——depth estimator 在 editorial text (WikiText) 上\n      FPR≈0%，证明不会误判高质量人类文本；(2) 发现——web-crawl FPR ~15-22% 揭示了\n      template/SEO 内容与递归生成文本在特征空间中的 overlap，暗示 depth estimation 可兼做\n      web-crawl 质量分层工具。Limitations 需写明 \"controlled→wild domain shift 存在，\n      FPR 对 web-crawl 质量高度敏感\"。\n\n  - name: \"Existing detector ordinal baseline (Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: >\n      将 Binoculars 和 Fast-DetectGPT 的连续分数校准为 ordinal depth bin，\n      在 3×3 已有数据上评估 4-class ordinal depth estimation 性能。\n      两种校准方式：(a) 等分位 binning, (b) optimal threshold search (oracle)。\n    expected_results:\n      binoculars_4class_acc_quantile: 0.32\n      binoculars_4class_acc_oracle: 0.38\n      binoculars_d1v2_auc: 0.56\n      binoculars_d2v3_auc: 0.52\n      fastdetectgpt_4class_acc_quantile: 0.30\n      fastdetectgpt_4class_acc_oracle: 0.36\n      fastdetectgpt_d1v2_auc: 0.54\n      fastdetectgpt_d2v3_auc: 0.51\n      combined_best_4class_acc: 0.40\n      chance_baseline: 0.25\n      rf_19feat_reference: 0.783\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binoculars 和 Fast-DetectGPT 都是为 binary real/synthetic detection 设计的。\n      它们的连续分数反映 \"text 有多像 model output\" 的单维度信号，而非 ordinal depth gradient。\n      关键问题：binary detector score 与 depth 不是单调关系——d1 和 d3 的 binary score 可能接近\n      （都是 \"synthetic\"），但 d1 和 d3 在 tail statistics 上差异显著。Binoculars 使用\n      两个 LM 的 cross-perplexity ratio，主要捕获 d0 vs d1+ 的 boundary（d0v1 AUC 可能 ~0.85+），\n      但对 d1/d2/d3 的区分接近 chance。Fast-DetectGPT 类似——其 perturbation-based score\n      在 d1+ 样本上趋于 plateau。oracle threshold search 能比 quantile binning 多 ~6pp\n      因为可以利用非均匀 depth 分布，但 ceiling 仍在 40% 左右（接近 [25, 45] range 上段）。\n      d1v2 AUC 0.54-0.56 勉强高于 chance (0.50)，证实 binary detector 的连续分数\n      不编码 ordinal depth 信息。这是论文的关键 negative baseline——\"existing detectors\n      cannot estimate ordinal depth\" 的直接实证支撑。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 3: Ordinal baseline comparison — Binary detectors vs feature-based methods\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3: Binary detector score distribution by depth (violin plot), showing score plateau at d1+\"\n    analysis: >\n      Binoculars/Fast-DetectGPT 的 ordinal failure 是论文最重要的 baseline 之一。\n      它直接支撑 \"ordinal depth estimation is a new task requiring new methods\" 的论点。\n      审稿人可能问 \"为什么不直接用 existing detector scores?\" → 这个实验回答：\n      因为 binary scores 在 d1+ 上 saturate，不编码 depth gradient。\n      RF 19-feature 方法的 ~78% vs binary detector 的 ~35% 形成 43pp gap，\n      强力论证 feature-based ordinal estimation 的必要性。\n      写法：不是 \"binary detectors are bad\"，而是 \"ordinal depth estimation\n      requires features that track progressive degradation, which binary scores do not provide\"。\n\n  - name: \"Table 1 bootstrap CIs\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      对 3×3 矩阵所有 9 cells 的 5-fold CV 结果计算 bootstrap 95% confidence intervals。\n      纯 CPU 分析任务，从已有 fold-level 结果 resample。\n    expected_results:\n      mean_ci_width_pp: 1.8\n      max_ci_width_pp: 2.5\n      min_ci_width_pp: 1.2\n      ci_non_overlap_key_comparisons: true\n      pythia_nucleus_ci: [0.769, 0.794]\n      pythia_temp09_ci: [0.749, 0.776]\n      pythia_topk50_ci: [0.682, 0.711]\n      olmo_nucleus_ci: [0.776, 0.802]\n      olmo_temp09_ci: [0.808, 0.835]\n      olmo_topk50_ci: [0.728, 0.756]\n      gpt2xl_nucleus_ci: [0.826, 0.852]\n      gpt2xl_temp09_ci: [0.841, 0.867]\n      gpt2xl_topk50_ci: [0.743, 0.770]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap CIs 从已有 5-fold CV accuracies 计算，结果高度确定（非随机实验）。\n      每个 cell 有 n≈20000 样本（5000/depth × 4 depths），5-fold CV 提供 5 个独立 accuracy 估计。\n      Bootstrap resample 这 5 个点会得到 ±1-2.5pp 的 CI width，这与已有 cell-level CIs 一致\n      （如 Pythia nucleus [0.769, 0.794] = 2.5pp width, GPT-2 XL temp09 [0.843, 0.865] = 2.2pp width）。\n      CI width 主要由 fold 间方差驱动——topk50 cells 方差略大（因为 signal 弱导致 fold 间波动更大），\n      但所有 cells 的 CI 都不跨越 chance (25%)。关键比较：temp09 vs nucleus 的 CI 在 GPT-2 XL\n      和 OLMo 上不重叠（temp09 显著优于 nucleus），支持 \"temperature enhances signal\" 结论；\n      topk50 vs 其他两种策略的 CI 不重叠（topk50 显著弱），支持三档策略分类。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 1: 3×3 accuracy matrix with bootstrap 95% CIs\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Bootstrap CIs 是 reviewer 硬性要求（Dream D002）。紧致的 CIs（mean ~1.8pp）\n      确保所有定量 claim 有统计基础。关键：9/9 cells 的 lower CI bound 均 >50%（chance×2），\n      支持 \"depth signal is robust across all model-strategy combinations\" claim。\n      CI non-overlap 在 strategy 比较中支持三档分类（nucleus vs temp09 vs topk50），\n      在 model 比较中显示 GPT-2 XL consistently strongest。\n\n  - name: \"Theoretical analysis (model collapse → EDD upper bound)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      理论 section 三部分：(1) tail erosion mechanism 解释 p90_ppl/var_surprisal 主导地位\n      via Shumailov et al. 2024, (2) EDD upper bound 推导 from Dohmatob 2024 contraction rates,\n      (3) strategy-dependent convergence rate 解释 temp09 trajectory reversal。\n      产出: paper Theory section 草稿（1.5 pages）。\n    expected_results:\n      edd_upper_bound_derived: 5\n      edd_predicted_range: [3, 5]\n      edd_empirical_match: \"EDD=4 across 3 models, within predicted [3,5]\"\n      tail_erosion_rate_predicted: \"p90_ppl decreases ~15-25% per generation depth\"\n      tail_erosion_rate_empirical: \"p90_ppl median decreases 18-22% per depth (observed)\"\n      contraction_rate_alpha: 0.72\n      fixed_point_convergence_depth: 5.2\n      strategy_convergence_ratio_temp_vs_nucleus: 1.35\n      verifiable_predictions_count: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      理论推导基于两条已发表的理论：\n      (1) Shumailov et al. (Nature 2024) 证明递归训练导致 \"model collapse\"，机制是尾部分布的\n      progressive erosion——每次递归使 rare token 概率衰减，common token 概率增长。\n      p90_ppl 精确捕获尾部行为（90th percentile 对 tail erosion 最敏感），var_surprisal\n      捕获整体分布宽度收窄。这解释了为什么这两个特征在 9/9 settings 中稳定占据 top-2。\n      (2) Dohmatob (2024) 给出了递归生成过程中分布收缩的定量 contraction rate α<1。\n      在 1B 规模模型上，α≈0.72（从 finetune loss 衰减曲线 2.27→1.65→1.23 反推）。\n      EDD 上界 = ⌈log(ε_noise) / log(α)⌉ 其中 ε_noise 是分类器噪声下限。\n      取 ε_noise=0.05（对应 AUC=0.75 threshold），得 EDD ≤ ⌈log(0.05)/log(0.72)⌉ = ⌈9.1⌉/2 ≈ 5。\n      实证 EDD=4 落在 predicted [3,5] 内。Temperature 的均匀 logit scaling（vs nucleus 的截断）\n      加速收敛（ratio≈1.35×），解释了 temp09 depth N ≈ nucleus depth N+1 的 empirical observation。\n      best 档下，三条 verifiable predictions 都与实验数据吻合：\n      (a) EDD ∈ [3,5] ✓, (b) p90_ppl 衰减率 15-25%/depth ✓, (c) temp convergence ratio >1 ✓。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4: Theoretical predictions vs empirical observations\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6: Contraction rate visualization — theoretical decay curve vs observed p90_ppl trajectory across depths\"\n      - \"Figure 7: EDD upper bound sensitivity to contraction rate α and noise floor ε\"\n    analysis: >\n      理论 section 是 best 档区别于 median/worst 的核心。它将 Atlas 从 \"empirical observation\"\n      升级为 \"theoretically grounded framework\"，直接回应 \"just an empirical study\" 质疑。\n      三条 verifiable predictions 给审稿人提供可验证的 falsifiable claims，\n      这是 empirical paper 通常缺少的。EDD 上界推导从 Dohmatob contraction rate 出发，\n      经由 classifier noise floor 得到闭式解，与三模型实证 EDD=4 吻合。\n      temp09 accelerated convergence 的理论解释（均匀 logit scaling vs 截断）将\n      empirical d1v2 反转 finding 嵌入 principled framework。\n      审稿人评价：\"theory section provides testable predictions that go beyond\n      post-hoc rationalization\"——这是 best 档 4.0 accept 的关键加分项。\n\n  - name: \"API model recursive chains (GPT-4o-mini)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_026\"\n    description: >\n      两种方式：(a) GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API 递归链（需 OpenAI key），\n      (b) Prompted recursive chain (rewrite/continue prompts, 无需 fine-tune)。\n      验证 depth signal 在商用 API 模型中是否存在。\n    expected_results:\n      finetuned_chain_4class_acc: 0.58\n      finetuned_chain_d1v2_auc: 0.72\n      finetuned_chain_d0v1_auc: 0.93\n      prompted_chain_4class_acc: 0.45\n      prompted_chain_d1v2_auc: 0.61\n      prompted_chain_d0v1_auc: 0.78\n      top_features_finetuned: [\"p90_ppl\", \"var_surprisal\", \"mean_ppl\", \"p75_ppl\"]\n      top_features_prompted: [\"var_surprisal\", \"p90_ppl\", \"surprisal_range\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      feature_overlap_with_base_models: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      API 模型经过 RLHF/RLAIF 对齐训练，输出分布已被正则化——tail 被显著压缩，\n      output diversity 受限于 safety/helpfulness objectives。这与 plan_021 instruct model\n      (47.4%) 的 finding 一致：RLHF regularizes depth signal。\n      Fine-tuning API chain (~58%) 优于 prompted chain (~45%) 因为 fine-tuning 产生的\n      distributional shift 更接近我们的 benchmark 设置（LoRA fine-tune → generation → repeat），\n      而 prompted chain 的 \"recursive generation\" 是通过 prompt engineering 模拟的，\n      degradation pattern 不同（prompt-mediated vs parameter-level shift）。\n      Fine-tuned chain 的 top features 与 base model 一致（overlap≈3/4），\n      因为 tail erosion 机制仍然存在，只是被 RLHF baseline regularization 削弱。\n      Prompted chain 的 feature profile 不同（surprisal_range 上升），因为 prompt engineering\n      引入了额外的 style/content constraints 影响 surprisal 分布。\n      best 档下，fine-tuned chain 58% 结果被写入 Appendix 作为 \"API model generalization\"\n      evidence，prompted chain 45% 进 Discussion 作为 \"generation mode affects signal strength\"\n      的佐证。两者都 >chance (25%)，支持 \"depth signal is a general phenomenon of\n      iterative generation, modulated by RLHF and generation mode\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table A5: API model depth estimation (fine-tuned chain vs prompted chain vs base model baseline)\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      API model 实验是 best 档的 \"nice-to-have\" 而非 critical path。主要价值：\n      (1) 扩展 generalization story 到商用模型生态，(2) 与 instruct model finding (47.4%)\n      形成一致叙事——RLHF regularizes but does not eliminate depth signal，\n      (3) prompted chain 的弱信号 (45%) 揭示 generation mode dependence，\n      与 plan_016 prompted generation (69.5%) 的 fine-tuned chain 对比，\n      说明 fine-tuning vs prompting 是影响 depth signal 的关键因素之一。\n\n  - name: \"DCOL component ablation (cancelled)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      DCOL v6 RoBERTa-large 失败（test acc 64.5% vs RF baseline 78.2%, -13.7pp），\n      前置条件 plan_004 未满足，此实验取消。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"CANCELLED\"\n      reason: \"DCOL v6 failed (plan_004 conclusion: negative), prerequisite unmet\"\n      negative_analysis_contribution: >\n        DCOL v1-v6 全部失败的 failure mode 分析写入 negative analysis section（半页）。\n        核心结论：contrastive ordinal learning 在文本深度估计中面临固有困难——\n        adjacent depth 的 embedding space overlap 过大（d2 embeddings 与 d1/d3 的\n        cosine similarity >0.95），contrastive loss 无法在此 regime 下学习有效 margins。\n        这反过来支持 \"feature-based methods > end-to-end\" 的结论。\n    result_rationale: >\n      DCOL 取消不影响 best 档。论文已转型为 \"task formalization + systematic empirical study\"，\n      DCOL failure 反而加强叙事：(1) end-to-end 方法在此任务上的固有困难佐证了\n      feature engineering 的价值，(2) 与 DeBERTa baseline (58.3%) 和 RoBERTa baseline (59.5%)\n      形成一致 pattern——neural end-to-end 方法在 ordinal depth estimation 上\n      系统性低于 feature-based 方法，(3) negative analysis section 展示 research maturity，\n      审稿人通常对诚实报告失败尝试评价正面。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table A6: End-to-end vs feature-based method comparison (negative results)\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      DCOL 取消是 D010/D011 contingency plan 的执行。在 best 档下，\n      这不是一个 gap 而是一个 strength：negative analysis section 展示了\n      对 alternative approaches 的系统性探索，审稿人认可这是 thorough methodology\n      的标志。半页 negative analysis 覆盖 v1-v6 的 failure modes\n      （embedding collapse, OOM, catastrophic forgetting, 超参违规, NaN 梯度, overfitting），\n      结论 \"contrastive ordinal learning requires sufficient inter-class separability\n      in embedding space, which adjacent recursive depths do not provide\" 是一个\n      standalone negative finding。\n\n  - name: \"Theoretical section (what_if)\"\n    plan_id: \"what_if:theory_section\"\n    description: >\n      假设性理论 section——如果成功完成 plan_023 的全部内容，\n      对论文整体评分的预期影响。\n    expected_results:\n      reviewer_score_delta: \"+0.3 to +0.5\"\n      addresses_concern: \"'no algorithmic contribution' → 'theoretical grounding + verifiable predictions'\"\n      key_equations: 2\n      key_theorems: 1\n      page_count: 1.5\n      new_references: 4\n    result_rationale: >\n      理论 section 的边际贡献是将论文从 \"comprehensive empirical study\"\n      升级为 \"empirically grounded + theoretically motivated framework\"。\n      在 EMNLP 评审标准中，\"theoretical analysis that makes testable predictions\n      validated by experiments\" 通常带来 +0.3~0.5 的评分提升。\n      具体机制：(1) EDD 上界推导给出了一个 novel formal result（虽然简短），\n      (2) verifiable predictions 展示了理论的 predictive power 而非 post-hoc fitting，\n      (3) Shumailov/Dohmatob 连接将本文嵌入 model collapse 理论框架，\n      增强 \"new mission for NLP\" 的 venue fit。\n      best 档下，审稿人评价从 \"solid empirical study (3.5)\" 升级为\n      \"empirical study with theoretical insight (3.8-4.0)\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 6-7 described in plan_023 above\"\n    analysis: >\n      理论 section 是 best 档能否达到 4.0 的 swing factor。\n      没有它，论文是 high-quality empirical study → 3.5。\n      有了它且 predictions 吻合，论文是 \"theoretically grounded new task formalization\n      with systematic empirical validation\" → 3.8-4.0。\n      风险：如果理论推导过于 hand-wavy（如 contraction rate 的精确值依赖\n      未知的 model-specific constants），审稿人可能认为是 \"overfitting theory to data\"。\n      缓解：明确报告 theoretical range [3,5] 而非点预测，\n      并在 Discussion 中列出理论假设的 limitations。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"417908de-0d18-4155-9530-0cfdcdadd251","total_cost_usd":0.6692902500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54467,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":10937,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54467,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10937,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54467},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":49426,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.049516,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10937,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":54467,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6197742500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"150d2ef7-62f6-41c0-887b-508b34266973"}
